WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.066
A sponsor can't sign off on
an outcome that has no test,

2
00:00:03.066 --> 00:00:06.853
so each of the charter's six success
criteria comes with a measure,

3
00:00:06.853 --> 00:00:10.150
the evidence that shows it, and
the gate where it's checked.

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.325
Two examples.

5
00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:16.476
The current-state assessment is done
when it covers every forest in scope and

6
00:00:16.476 --> 00:00:21.788
all eleven types of dependency, with no
open priority-one findings, checked at G0.

7
00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:25.562
And the target model is agreed
when every attribute that

8
00:00:25.562 --> 00:00:29.738
drives access has exactly one
designated source, checked at G1.

9
00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:34.854
The others cover a working pilot playbook,
change control on every pilot change,

10
00:00:34.854 --> 00:00:37.024
a response for every kind of drift,

11
00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:40.900
and leadership being able to
explain the path in plain terms.

12
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.100
The numbers are illustrative defaults.

13
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:48.762
The agency sets its own, writes them down,
and never quietly changes them later.

14
00:00:48.762 --> 00:00:53.160
And these criteria stop at the
pilot; Chapter 10 measures the rest.
